  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2022 Contribution to ICRC Ukraine Appeal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Armed conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">People affected by the conflict in Ukraine</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) expanded its presence in Ukraine in 2014, to help protect and assist conflict-affected people in the eastern part of the country. It is now scaling up its operations in response to the current situation, primarily in Ukraine but also in affected neighbouring countries in close coordination with the National Societies and the IFRC.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukraine and neighboring countries</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Urging respect for International Humanitarian Law; Supporting the continued functioning of essential infrastructure; Ensuring the availability of life-saving care and other health services; Helping people stay safe from weapon contamination; Assisting conflict-affected people in meeting their basic needs and recovering their livelihoods; Enabling people to contact their relatives or to ascertain their fate; Supporting and coordinating with Movement partners</narrative>
  </description>
